WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:08.848
&gt;&gt; Jane fonda has been a movie

00:00:09.115 --> 00:00:10.716
star for more than half a

00:00:10.983 --> 00:00:12.652
century, but when I ran a clip

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:14.654
from one of her most celebrated

00:00:14.921 --> 00:00:17.857
films, 1981's golden pond, in

00:00:17.924 --> 00:00:19.859
which she co start with her

00:00:19.926 --> 00:00:21.861
father, Henry fonda, I was

00:00:22.028 --> 00:00:23.930
surprised by her reaction.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:26.732
&gt;&gt; It seems that you and me

00:00:26.999 --> 00:00:27.867
have been mad at each other for

00:00:28.134 --> 00:00:28.734
so long.

00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:30.603
&gt;&gt; I did not know we were mad,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:31.871
I just thought we did not like

00:00:31.871 --> 00:00:34.106
each other.

00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:42.214
&gt;&gt; I want to be your friend.

00:00:42.481 --> 00:00:47.887
&gt;&gt; This means you will come

00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:50.590
around more often, unlike your

00:00:50.856 --> 00:00:50.990
mother?

00:00:51.891 --> 00:00:57.897
&gt;&gt; I will come around more

00:00:57.897 --> 00:00:57.997
often.

00:00:58.264 --> 00:01:00.666
&gt;&gt; You did not watch that scene,

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:01.067
why not?

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.737
&gt;&gt; Because it makes me cry.

00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:06.806
I miss my dad so much.

00:01:07.907 --> 00:01:09.909
&gt;&gt; That scene felt like more

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:10.977
than a scene in a movie.

00:01:12.678 --> 00:01:12.845
&gt;&gt; It was.

00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:16.649
&gt;&gt; You know, I love my dad and

00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:17.116
admire him.

00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:20.686
He was quite a bit like Norman,

00:01:20.953 --> 00:01:29.929
removed, not able to express --

00:01:29.962 --> 00:01:32.932
he always liked to do things

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:33.966
that were rehearsed a lot.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.936
I purposely did something that

00:01:37.203 --> 00:01:37.937
had not been rehearsed because

00:01:38.638 --> 00:01:41.941
I wanted him to be surprised.

00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:43.943
When I said, I want to be your

00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:45.945
friend and touch this arm, we

00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:47.947
had not rehearsed that.

00:01:48.114 --> 00:01:50.616
And he flinches, and he ducked

00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:51.951
his head and puts his hand like

00:01:52.118 --> 00:01:54.654
this, but I saw that he was

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.957
emotional.

00:01:57.957 --> 00:01:59.959
It's funny for an acted that

00:01:59.959 --> 00:02:01.961
does not want to be seen as a

00:02:01.994 --> 00:02:02.862
emotional, but he was terrified

00:02:03.129 --> 00:02:03.963
of emotions.

00:02:04.063 --> 00:02:05.965
That meant a lot to me.

00:02:06.699 --> 00:02:08.801
I went to his house, wanted to

00:02:09.068 --> 00:02:10.703
talk to him about the scene,

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.772
because I had a hard time with

00:02:13.039 --> 00:02:13.205
the scene.

00:02:13.973 --> 00:02:17.977
It was so personal that when we

00:02:17.977 --> 00:02:19.979
actually got there to do it, I

00:02:19.979 --> 00:02:24.717
totally dried up.

00:02:24.984 --> 00:02:26.819
It was like an actor's worst

00:02:27.086 --> 00:02:28.721
nightmare, and I asked them

00:02:28.988 --> 00:02:29.989
afterwards at dinner, has that

00:02:30.056 --> 00:02:30.723
ever happened to?

00:02:32.658 --> 00:02:35.995
No, no, that's it.

00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:37.997
I could not get into --

00:02:38.064 --> 00:02:42.001
&gt;&gt; How was it to love this man,

00:02:42.034 --> 00:02:44.003
and for him, it's part of

00:02:44.036 --> 00:02:46.005
Hollywood lore, we all read

00:02:46.005 --> 00:02:48.007
about, he was so emotionally

00:02:48.107 --> 00:02:48.674
beholden.

00:02:48.941 --> 00:02:50.009
I would think that would be

00:02:50.776 --> 00:02:50.876
tough.

00:02:51.143 --> 00:02:52.011
&gt;&gt; Well, it is.

00:02:52.078 --> 00:02:54.013
It is very common, especially

00:02:54.113 --> 00:02:56.849
for women my age, or boys and

00:02:57.116 --> 00:02:59.685
girls my age, not just women,

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:01.654
whose fathers were of that

00:03:02.021 --> 00:03:04.657
generation, and especially

00:03:04.924 --> 00:03:05.124
mid-western.

00:03:06.025 --> 00:03:08.694
There was a certain attitude,

00:03:08.961 --> 00:03:10.730
like, you don't ever ask

00:03:10.996 --> 00:03:12.031
anything, don't express need,

00:03:12.198 --> 00:03:14.767
and you stifle your emotions.

00:03:15.034 --> 00:03:17.670
Of course, when a figure of

00:03:18.037 --> 00:03:19.672
your love is withholding and

00:03:20.039 --> 00:03:23.609
repressed, it has an impact on

00:03:24.043 --> 00:03:25.711
a kid and their relationships

00:03:26.045 --> 00:03:26.712
after they grow up.

00:03:26.979 --> 00:03:28.681
I've been married three times.

00:03:29.715 --> 00:03:32.051
I did not have a good hand that

00:03:32.051 --> 00:03:32.885
to me when it comes to

00:03:33.152 --> 00:03:35.654
relationships.

00:03:36.055 --> 00:03:37.690
&gt;&gt; We were both crazy enough,

00:03:38.057 --> 00:03:41.727
potion off to follow our famous

00:03:42.061 --> 00:03:42.661
fathers into their professions.

00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:44.063
Did you resolve things with

00:03:44.263 --> 00:03:45.131
your father before the end of

00:03:45.664 --> 00:03:49.735
his life?

00:03:52.772 --> 00:03:56.776
&gt;&gt; That movie on golden pond

00:03:57.042 --> 00:03:59.712
was kind of like a resolution,

00:04:00.079 --> 00:04:00.146
in a way.

00:04:00.679 --> 00:04:02.081
My being able to say that to

00:04:02.114 --> 00:04:06.685
him in the scene, and he died

00:04:06.952 --> 00:04:08.087
five months later, and before

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.756
he died, I was able to tell him

00:04:11.023 --> 00:04:15.094
that I loved him --

00:04:17.763 --> 00:04:20.099
the I forgave him for whatever

00:04:20.332 --> 00:04:22.902
it did not happen, and I hope

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:24.103
that he would forgive me for

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.105
not being a better daughter.

00:04:26.739 --> 00:04:28.774
I got to say that to him.

00:04:29.041 --> 00:04:32.778
He did not say anything, but he

00:04:33.045 --> 00:04:36.949
wept, and I had never seen that

00:04:37.216 --> 00:04:37.349
before.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.752
I never seen my father

00:04:40.119 --> 00:04:41.754
breakdown in front of me.

00:04:43.756 --> 00:04:44.123
It was powerful.

00:04:44.857 --> 00:04:46.725
&gt;&gt; I have to say, I think it's

00:04:46.992 --> 00:04:48.127
one of the greatest gifts.

00:04:48.828 --> 00:04:50.129
I had a challenging

00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:52.131
relationship with my dad at

00:04:52.198 --> 00:04:54.133
various points, and he lived

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.137
long enough that we made it up

00:04:58.137 --> 00:05:00.139
and became best friends.

00:05:00.739 --> 00:05:02.141
I always felt that was such a

00:05:02.174 --> 00:05:02.908
gift because I cannot imagine

00:05:03.175 --> 00:05:04.777
going through life after it's

00:05:05.044 --> 00:05:06.946
too late and not having that

00:05:07.213 --> 00:05:07.379
resolved.

00:05:07.813 --> 00:05:09.748
&gt;&gt; It's so important to try to

00:05:10.149 --> 00:05:10.816
clear everything up before you

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:11.150
go.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.153
I am not scared of dying, are

00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:14.186
you?

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.155
&gt;&gt; I am not looking forward to

00:05:16.222 --> 00:05:16.288
it.

00:05:16.922 --> 00:05:18.157
&gt;&gt; I am.

00:05:18.157 --> 00:05:20.159
It's an adventure.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:22.828
I don't want to go, I still

00:05:23.095 --> 00:05:28.734
have a lot to do, but if I

00:05:29.001 --> 00:05:30.769
discovered that I had cancer

00:05:31.036 --> 00:05:32.171
again, and there was nothing I

00:05:32.271 --> 00:05:33.806
could do, I would be okay with

00:05:34.173 --> 00:05:34.406
it.

00:05:34.406 --> 00:05:36.175
What I am really scared of is

00:05:36.208 --> 00:05:37.109
getting to the end of life with

00:05:37.376 --> 00:05:38.978
a lot of regrets, when there is

00:05:39.245 --> 00:05:40.846
no time to do anything about

00:05:41.113 --> 00:05:41.180
it.

00:05:41.747 --> 00:05:44.817
It's one reason that I try to

00:05:45.084 --> 00:05:45.117
--

00:05:45.384 --> 00:05:46.752
I am trying to get it all done

00:05:47.019 --> 00:05:48.187
before I come to the end.

00:05:48.821 --> 00:05:50.189
&gt;&gt; But do you have regrets?

00:05:50.189 --> 00:05:52.191
I would think that you would be

00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:54.193
somebody that feels pretty good

00:05:54.226 --> 00:05:54.360
about --

00:05:54.693 --> 00:05:56.929
&gt;&gt; I have very few regrets.

00:05:57.763 --> 00:05:59.832
I was not the kind of mother

00:06:00.199 --> 00:06:00.833
that I wished I had been to my

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:02.935
children, but I have great,

00:06:03.202 --> 00:06:05.804
great children, talented, smart,

00:06:06.205 --> 00:06:08.207
and I just did not know how to

00:06:08.274 --> 00:06:09.775
do it.

00:06:10.209 --> 00:06:12.811
You know, I have an

00:06:13.078 --> 00:06:14.847
organization in Georgia that

00:06:15.114 --> 00:06:17.850
deals with adolescents, and I

00:06:18.217 --> 00:06:18.984
studied parenting.

00:06:19.251 --> 00:06:20.219
I know what it is supposed to

00:06:20.719 --> 00:06:20.819
be no.

00:06:21.086 --> 00:06:22.221
I did not know than.

00:06:22.221 --> 00:06:23.055
I am trying to show up now.

00:06:23.722 --> 00:06:25.824
&gt;&gt; Jane, I got to say, this is

00:06:26.225 --> 00:06:27.159
quite a conversation we're

00:06:27.793 --> 00:06:28.227
having here.

00:06:28.761 --> 00:06:30.229
This is real, which is exactly

00:06:30.296 --> 00:06:32.798
what I am looking for.

00:06:33.065 --> 00:06:33.899
&gt;&gt; I hate parties.

00:06:34.733 --> 00:06:36.235
I hate cocktail parties.

00:06:36.769 --> 00:06:38.971
I always end up finding one

00:06:39.238 --> 00:06:41.006
person that is interesting and

00:06:41.273 --> 00:06:42.241
sitting and a corner all night.

00:06:42.741 --> 00:06:42.975
Do you do the?

00:06:43.809 --> 00:06:45.010
&gt;&gt; I know what you're saying.

00:06:45.277 --> 00:06:47.780
&gt;&gt; Because I am shy, basically.

00:06:48.814 --> 00:06:50.916
Just small talk, I can't do it,

00:06:51.183 --> 00:06:52.251
isn't that boring?

00:06:52.284 --> 00:06:53.919
&gt;&gt; I want to ask you a couple

00:06:54.253 --> 00:06:55.854
of other questions.

00:06:56.255 --> 00:06:59.758
As you say, you were married

00:07:00.259 --> 00:07:00.893
three times to three very

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:01.393
different men.

00:07:01.827 --> 00:07:03.829
French film director Roger --

00:07:04.797 --> 00:07:06.932
Tom Hayden, the anti war

00:07:07.199 --> 00:07:09.768
activists and of course, Tom

00:07:10.269 --> 00:07:10.903
Warner, who created CNN.

00:07:11.737 --> 00:07:12.905
You set much of your life, you

00:07:13.172 --> 00:07:15.908
turned two men for guidance and

00:07:16.275 --> 00:07:17.109
validation, is that because you

00:07:17.443 --> 00:07:19.778
did not get it from you that?

00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:22.281
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I suppose, and the

00:07:22.414 --> 00:07:23.882
fact that my mother killed

00:07:24.283 --> 00:07:25.818
herself when I was 12.

00:07:26.285 --> 00:07:31.857
You know, I just assumed that

00:07:32.291 --> 00:07:34.293
nobody would be interesting and

00:07:34.293 --> 00:07:35.828
knowing me unless I was with a

00:07:36.295 --> 00:07:37.863
man who is interesting, and

00:07:38.297 --> 00:07:38.998
they were all interesting.

00:07:39.732 --> 00:07:41.734
&gt;&gt; When did that change for you,

00:07:42.301 --> 00:07:44.803
when did you realize that, one,

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:48.307
I, Jane fonda is interesting

00:07:48.307 --> 00:07:52.811
and, to, I don't need a man?

00:07:53.746 --> 00:08:00.719
&gt;&gt; When Ted turner and I split

00:08:00.986 --> 00:08:04.323
in 2000, started a new century

00:08:04.323 --> 00:08:08.994
on my own, and I kind of

00:08:09.261 --> 00:08:13.732
thought, oh, I am single and I

